WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.650
A prediction error first needs a reference: prediction minus observed target. That signed residual tells you

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:13.101
whether a model is too high or too low. Averaging signed residuals can conceal mistakes because

00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:14.310
opposite signs cancel.

00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:20.143
A residual is prediction minus target. Its sign tells us the direction of the error.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:25.857
The square treats equal positive and negative mistakes equally and prevents cancellation.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:31.901
Will reversing the sign change the mean squared error? Pause here and make a prediction before

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:32.247
continuing.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:41.140
The denominator is the number of residuals, including zero residuals. It is not the number of

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:47.457
mistakes. For our starting inputs, Signed residual: -2. Squared-error sum: 4. MSE: 1.3333.

00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:52.837
Doubling errors quadruples squared error. Loss units are the square of the target units.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:59.599
A loss can become smaller through better predictions or simply through rescaling the target. Compare models

00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:01.937
under the same objective and units.

